"deltaSeconds":421}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":13,"finishersRank":22,"finishRateRank":97,"winningTimeRank":30,"winningTimeRankDir":11,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1959,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"06:28:11"}},"narrative":"The 2011 Comrades Marathon was the 86th running of the race, run in the 'up' direction from Durban to Pietermaritzburg over 86.940 km. The race was held on Sunday, 29 May. Conditions: Mild morning. Warm sunshine, but cooling to cold late afternoon. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nStephen MUZHINGI claimed the men's title in 05:32:46, ahead of Fanie MATSHIPA (05:34:30) and Claude MOSHIYWA (05:42:06). Elena NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:24:11, followed by Olesya NURGALIEVA (06:24:36).\n\nElena NURGALIEVA's 06:24:11 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1959 (Trevor ALLEN, 06:28:11).\n\nFrom a field of 19,541 entries, 11,060 runners crossed the finish line (56.6% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 8,877 men and 2,183 women (19.7% female). The average finish time was 10:16:08.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 4 Wally Hayward, 447 Silver, 1,717 Bill Rowan, 5,254 Bronze, 3,618 Vic Clapham. 2,449 runners (22.1%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Sbusiso NTULI in 11:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 2008, the field was 74.7% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 54% of the finishers, with 5,086 seniors (avg 10:01:02) and 5,973 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}